        "original_id": "85c0e3f5-fb5f-5167-a4d8-5173cf87a5ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Hirohito, Hideo Kanaya\n- Concepts: Wet-folding, Shōwa era, Order of the Rising Sun\n- Topics: Origami, Japanese honors, Motorcycle racing\n\nFacts:\n- Hirohito's reign corresponded to the Shōwa era, and Shōwa became his own name after his death.\n- Hideo Kanaya was born on February 3, 1945, and he was a Japanese Grand Prix motorcycle road racer.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- Hideo Kanaya died on December 19, 2013.",
